---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "@/config/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Standards"
  description="How Toolsiva approaches practical tool guides, AI-assisted drafts, factual corrections, advertising and editorial transparency."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:py-16">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-brand-300">Transparency</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-white sm:text-4xl">Editorial standards</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
      Toolsiva combines browser-based utilities with practical guides that explain what a tool
      does, how to use it and when its results need independent verification.
    </p>

    <div class="prose-premium mt-10 space-y-10 text-sm leading-7 text-zinc-300">
      <section>
        <h2>Practical information comes first</h2>
        <p>
          A guide should help readers solve a concrete task. We aim to include examples that can
          be reproduced with the related tool, explain meaningful limitations and link only to
          relevant supporting resources. Tool availability does not guarantee that any particular
          output is suitable for high-stakes decisions.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>AI-assisted draft review</h2>
        <p>
          Toolsiva may use generative AI to help prepare drafts. As of November 15, 2026, the
          automated guide workflow produces unpublished AI-assisted drafts for editorial review rather than
          publishing them immediately. A draft needs its claims, examples, originality, relevance,
          links and actual tool behavior reviewed before its status is changed to published.
          Existing articles may be revised as this review process develops.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Accuracy and revisions</h2>
        <p>
          Software and standards can change. Calculator assumptions, encoding formats, browser
          behavior and security advice are not universally interchangeable. We aim to correct
          reproducible errors and make meaningful updates visible through revised article dates,
          without altering dates just to imply freshness.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Advertising independence</h2>
        <p>
          Toolsiva does not currently display third-party advertisements. If advertising is
          introduced, advertisements should be distinguishable from tool controls and editorial
          information, and the Privacy Policy will be updated to reflect applicable data use and
          consent practices. Payment or advertising should not determine a calculation's output.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Questions and corrections</h2>
        <p>
          To report a mistake, please include the page URL, sample input, expected result and
          actual result. Send feedback to
          <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>.
          You can also review our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
